# Generated C header line-ending pin.
#
# include/slipstream_core.h is written by crates/slipstream-core/build.rs, which
# emits LF endings. With core.autocrlf=true Git expects CRLF in the working tree,
# so every build rewrote the file and left `git status` reporting it as modified
# with an empty diff. Pinning this path to LF makes the generator output and the
# checkout agree, so a build no longer dirties the tree.
#
# Path-scoped deliberately: this says nothing about any other file.
include/slipstream_core.h text eol=lf
